            "text": "For most healthy adults, yes, in moderation. The flagship gives about 21 g of organic plant protein for roughly 150 calories with under 1 g of sugar and useful fiber. The caveat is lead: Consumer Reports' 2025 testing put it above its daily level of concern per serving, so we suggest using it a few times a week rather than as a twice-daily staple."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Orgain protein powder have lead?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Consumer Reports' October 2025 investigation measured Orgain Organic Plant-Based Protein Powder at about 143% of its 0.5 microgram daily level of concern for lead per serving and listed it as fine to have occasionally through the week. Lead in plant protein comes mainly from soil. Pregnant readers and parents should talk to a doctor before daily use."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much protein is in Orgain protein powder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The flagship Organic Protein Plant-Based and the Grass-Fed Whey each give about 21 g of protein per two-scoop serving, per the label. Orgain Simple gives about 20 g, and the organic vegan 30g powder, sold as Orgain Sport at some stores, gives about 30 g. Figures vary slightly by flavor, so check the panel on your tub."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Orgain protein good for building muscle?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can help, but the 21 g serving is on the low side for a post-workout dose, and plant protein has less leucine per gram than whey. Lifters should choose the 30 g vegan powder, the Grass-Fed Whey with a little extra milk, or a higher-dose whey isolate. Total daily protein matters more than any single shake."
          }
        },
